Solar_Flare said:
If it's happening when the enemy is
near
the player, then I doubt it's related to the size of the map. Can you be more clear about what you mean by "randomly stutters and stops"?
Click to expand...
I have two versions, one with autorun on a separate Event and one that triggers when the player steps on a field:
I used
TheOdie's
script with $gamePlayer coords and once with separate values:
//This somewhat solves the "getting stuck in place" part but makes the enemies hug the walls
$gameMap._events[this._eventId].moveStraight($gameMap._events[this._eventId].findDirectionTo(
$gamePlayer.x,$gamePlayer.y
));
//This made the enemies slightly smarter but they tend to stop randomly right next to the player
$gameMap._events[this._eventId].moveStraight($gameMap._events[this._eventId].findDirectionTo(
$gameVariables.value(213),$gameVariables.value(214)
));
I hope the screenshots and videos suffice. Thank you!

drylilac said:
The thing is, I already tried that and even separate values but the enemy just randomly stutters and stops near the player a lot of the time for whatever reason. I guess my map is just "too big" so it breaks automatically.
Click to expand...
a better way is using this (which I made a mini plugin out of it
JavaScript:
Game_Character.prototype.chasePlayer = function() {
    $gameMap._events[this._eventId].moveStraight($gameMap._events[this._eventId].findDirectionTo($gamePlayer.x, $gamePlayer.y));
};

Game_Character.prototype.chasePlayerVariables = function(vx, vy) {
    $gameMap._events[this._eventId].moveStraight($gameMap._events[this._eventId].findDirectionTo($gameVariables.value(vx), $gameVariables.value(vy)));
};
this in a way the event wont get stuck as your gif.
use it like
this.chasePlayer()
or
this.chasePlayerVariables(vx, vy)
and your good to go, so it can work with this plugin without issue, save the above in a plugin.
as its just a snippet I made, and shared in one of the threads as plugin.

